      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we align with the other implementations, we will be relying on `set_active_device(nil)` to ensure that `end_session` is invoked and `pending_cmd_` is cleared.\n\nHowever, the bug being consistently reproducible is when headset initiates disconnection: `stop_request` -\u003e `end_session` -\u003e (notifies the audio stack). From here, if the audio stack calls `stop_request`, the command gets hung, but even if we called another `end_session` it will not solve the issue because it had been called previously and will be skipped.\n\nThus it seems best to block `stop_request` right away if we know that there is no active device to stop.",
      "parentUuid": "873e02d1_52b88e3e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 24,
        "startChar": 46,
